      "text": "```json\n{\"unit_id\": \"Nefertiti\", \"choices\": [\"C1\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Nfr.t-jy.tj ('the beautiful one has come'): nfr.t + jy.tj. 'Nefertiti' reads Nefer-t (nfr.t), i (jy), ti (.tj), so it renders exactly these words, and the TLA gives Nofretete. Same name. C2 Nfr.t-jy.tj-nfr-nfr.w-Jtn: the long form adds nfr-nfr.w-Jtn (Neferneferuaten). Record 1 has none of those consonants, and that is not an allowed omission, so it is a different, longer name. C3 Nfr.t-tw (Neferet-tu): its consonants n-f-r-t-t-w could just fit 'Nefertiti' if w is rendered as i. But its second word is tw, a different word from jy.tj 'has come'. As a modern spelling, 'Nefertiti' is the conventional rendering of nfr.t-jy.tj, not of nfr.t-tw, so the words differ and this is not the same name.\"}\n```"
